Shared content blocks (WI-501) live here, one Markdown fragment per file.

A curated page includes one with a line whose entire content is the block
name in brackets: [CROSSWALK] pulls in crosswalk.md.

Rules:
  - No title, no slug, no disclaimers. A block is a fragment of a page, not
    a page, and is never served on its own.
  - Front matter is optional and may carry only `sources`. Those merge into
    the front matter of every page that includes the block, so the block's
    sources live in one place too.
  - ContentCheck grades the COMPOSED page. A block is never graded alone,
    because a fragment can sit under 6.0 on its own while the assembled page
    goes over it.
  - A block no page includes is reported as a warning: nothing grades it.

Shipped blocks:
  - caregiver.md — the caregiver section every tumor hub carries (WI-558).
    See content-pipeline.md §12.7 for what belongs here and what belongs on
    the page around it.

Still to come: the retired-name crosswalk, written by WI-513 together with the
tumor page that includes it.
